"k": "kai/"}, {"t": "αὐτόματός", "o": 35, "k": "au)to/matos"}, {"t": "τις", "o": 45, "k": "tis"}]}, {"n": 30, "text": "εἶναι φορὰ τοῦ πνεύματος ἔξω· εἰ δὲ καὶ εἴσω, σκεπτέον.", "tokens": [{"t": "εἶναι", "o": 0, "k": "ei)=nai"}, {"t": "φορὰ", "o": 6, "k": "fora/"}, {"t": "τοῦ", "o": 11, "k": "tou="}, {"t": "πνεύματος", "o": 15, "k": "pneu/matos"}, {"t": "ἔξω", "o": 25, "k": "e)/cw"}, {"t": "εἰ", "o": 30, "k": "ei)"}, {"t": "δὲ", "o": 33, "k": "de/"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 36, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "εἴσω", "o": 40, "k": "ei)/sw"}, {"t": "σκεπτέον", "o": 46, "k": "skepte/on"}]}, {"n": 31, "text": "ἔοικε δέ· ὁμοίως γὰρ ἀναπνοὴν ποιοῦσι τοῖς κολυμβηταῖς", "tokens": [{"t": "ἔοικε", "o": 0, "k": "e)/oike"}, {"t": "δέ", "o": 6, "k": "de/"}, {"t": "ὁμοίως", "o": 10, "k": "o(moi/ws"}, {"t": "γὰρ", "o": 17, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "ἀναπνοὴν", "o": 21, "k": "a)napnoh/n"}, {"t": "ποιοῦσι", "o": 30, "k": "poiou=si"}, {"t": "τοῖς", "o": 38, "k": "toi=s"}, {"t": "κολυμβηταῖς", "o": 43, "k": "kolumbhtai=s"}]}, {"n": 32, "text": "λέβητα καταφέντες. οὐ πίμπλαται γὰρ οὗτος τοῦ ὕδατος,", "tokens": [{"t": "λέβητα", "o": 0, "k": "le/bhta"}, {"t": "καταφέντες", "o": 7, "k": "katafe/ntes"}, {"t": "οὐ", "o": 19, "k": "ou)"}, {"t": "πίμπλαται", "o": 22, "k": "pi/mplatai"}, {"t": "γὰρ", "o": 32, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "οὗτος", "o": 36, "k": "ou(=tos"}, {"t": "τοῦ", "o": 42, "k": "tou="}, {"t": "ὕδατος", "o": 46, "k": "u(/datos"}]}, {"n": 33, "text": "ἀλλὰ τηρεῖ τὸν ἀέρα. μετὰ βίας γὰρ ἡ κάθεσις. ὀρθὸν", "tokens": [{"t": "ἀλλὰ", "o": 0, "k": "a)lla/"}, {"t": "τηρεῖ", "o": 5, "k": "threi="}, {"t": "τὸν", "o": 11, "k": "to/n"}, {"t": "ἀέρα", "o": 15, "k": "a)e/ra"}, {"t": "μετὰ", "o": 21, "k": "meta/"}, {"t": "βίας", "o": 26, "k": "bi/as"}, {"t": "γὰρ", "o": 31, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "ἡ", "o": 35, "k": "h("}, {"t": "κάθεσις", "o": 37, "k": "ka/qesis"}, {"t": "ὀρθὸν", "o": 46, "k": "o)rqo/n"}]}, {"n": 34, "text": "γὰρ ὁτιοῦν παρεγκλιθὲν εἰσρεῖ.", "tokens": [{"t": "γὰρ", "o": 0, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "ὁτιοῦν", "o": 4, "k": "o(tiou=n"}, {"t": "παρεγκλιθὲν", "o": 11, "k": "paregkliqe/n"}, {"t": "εἰσρεῖ", "o": 23, "k": "ei)srei="}]}, {"n": 35, "text": "Διὰ τί ἔνιοι τὰ ὦτα σκαλεύοντες βήττουσιν; ἢ ὅτι ἐπὶ", "tokens": [{"t": "Διὰ", "o": 0, "k": "dia/"}, {"t": "τί", "o": 4, "k": "ti/"}, {"t": "ἔνιοι", "o": 7, "k": "e)/nioi"}, {"t": "τὰ", "o": 13, "k": "ta/"}, {"t": "ὦτα", "o": 16, "k": "w)=ta"}, {"t": "σκαλεύοντες", "o": 20, "k": "skaleu/ontes"}, {"t": "βήττουσιν", "o": 32, "k": "bh/ttousin"}, {"t": "ἢ", "o": 43, "k": "h)/"}, {"t": "ὅτι", "o": 45, "k": "o(/ti"}, {"t": "ἐπὶ", "o": 49, "k": "e)pi/"}]}, {"n": 36, "text": "τοῦ αὐτοῦ πόρου τῷ πνεύμονι καὶ τῇ ἀρτηρίᾳ ἡ ἀκοή; σημεῖον", "tokens": [{"t": "τοῦ", "o": 0, "k": "tou="}, {"t": "αὐτοῦ", "o": 4, "k": "au)tou="}, {"t": "πόρου", "o": 10, "k": "po/rou"}, {"t": "τῷ", "o": 16, "k": "tw=|"}, {"t": "πνεύμονι", "o": 19, "k": "pneu/moni"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 28, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "τῇ", "o": 32, "k": "th=|"}, {"t": "ἀρτηρίᾳ", "o": 35, "k": "a)rthri/a|"}, {"t": "ἡ", "o": 43, "k": "h("}, {"t": "ἀκοή", "o": 45, "k": "a)koh/"}, {"t": "σημεῖον", "o": 51, "k": "shmei=on"}]}, {"n": 37, "text": "δέ, ὅτι ἀναπηροῦνται καὶ γίνονται ἐνεοί. θερμαινομένου οὖν τῇ", "tokens": [{"t": "δέ", "o": 0, "k": "de/"}, {"t": "ὅτι", "o": 4, "k": "o(/ti"}, {"t": "ἀναπηροῦνται", "o": 8, "k": "a)naphrou=ntai"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 21, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "γίνονται", "o": 25, "k": "gi/nontai"}, {"t": "ἐνεοί", "o": 34, "k": "e)neoi/"}, {"t": "θερμαινομένου", "o": 41, "k": "qermainome/nou"}, {"t": "οὖν", "o": 55, "k": "ou)=n"}, {"t": "τῇ", "o": 59, "k": "th=|"}]}, {"n": 38, "text": "τρίψει συντήκεται ἐπὶ τὴν ἀρτηρίαν ἀπὸ τοῦ πόνου κάτωθεν", "tokens": [{"t": "τρίψει", "o": 0, "k": "tri/yei"}, {"t": "συντήκεται", "o": 7, "k": "sunth/ketai"}, {"t": "ἐπὶ", "o": 18, "k": "e)pi/"}, {"t": "τὴν", "o": 22, "k": "th/n"}, {"t": "ἀρτηρίαν", "o": 26, "k": "a)rthri/an"}, {"t": "ἀπὸ", "o": 35, "k": "a)po/"}, {"t": "τοῦ", "o": 39, "k": "tou="}, {"t": "πόνου", "o": 43, "k": "po/nou"}, {"t": "κάτωθεν", "o": 49, "k": "ka/twqen"}]}, {"n": 39, "text": "ὑγρόν· ὃ ποιεῖ τὴν βῆχα.", "tokens": [{"t": "ὑγρόν", "o": 0, "k": "u(gro/n"}, {"t": "ὃ", "o": 7, "k": "o(/"}, {"t": "ποιεῖ", "o": 9, "k": "poiei="}, {"t": "τὴν", "o": 15, "k": "th/n"}, {"t": "βῆχα", "o": 19, "k": "bh=xa"}]}, {"n": 40, "text": "Διὰ τί τὸ ἀριστερὸν οὖς θᾶττον συμφύεται ὡς ἐπὶ τὸ", "tokens": [{"t": "Διὰ", "o": 0, "k": "dia/"}, {"t": "τί", "o": 4, "k": "ti/"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 7, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "ἀριστερὸν", "o": 10, "k": "a)ristero/n"}, {"t": "οὖς", "o": 20, "k": "ou)=s"}, {"t": "θᾶττον", "o": 24, "k": "qa=tton"}, {"t": "συμφύεται", "o": 31, "k": "sumfu/etai"}, {"t": "ὡς", "o": 41, "k": "w(s"}, {"t": "ἐπὶ", "o": 44, "k": "e)pi/"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 48, "k": "to/"}]}], "english": {"text": "are near the temples, where the moisture most collects? Now under the emotion of shame the moisture flows into the face and causes blushing. But the ears have less depth than any other part of the face and are naturally very warm and fresh coloured, unless they have been long numbed by the cold; they are then the most fresh coloured of all the parts of the face, and so the heat, when it is dispersed, being nearest the surface in the ears, makes them red. Why is it that the ear-drums of divers burst in the sea? Is it because the ear, as it fills with water, is subject to violent pressure, because it retains the breath? Surely, if this is the reason, the same thing ought to happen in the air. Or is it because a thing breaks more easily if it does not yield, and more readily under pressure from what is hard than from what is soft? Now that which is inflated is less yielding, and the ears, as has been said, are inflated because the breath is retained in them; and so the water, which is harder than the air, when it presses upon them bursts them. Why do divers tie sponges round their ears? Is it in order that the sea may not rush violently in and burst the ear-drums? For thus the ears do not become full, as they do when the sponges are removed. Why is the dirt in the ears bitter? Is it because sweat is corrupt? It is, therefore, a salty, corrupt substance; and that which is corrupt and salty is bitter. Why do sponge-divers slit their ears and nostrils? Is it in order that the breath may pass more freely? For it is by this way that the breath seems to pass out; for it is said that they suffer more from difficulty of breathing by being unable to expel the breath, and they are relieved when they can as it were vomit the breath forth. It is strange, then, that they cannot achieve respiration for the sake of its cooling effect; this appears to be a greater necessity. Is it not quite natural that the strain should be greater when the breath is held, since then they are swollen and distended? But there appears to be a spontaneous passage of the breath outwards; and we must next consider whether breathing inwards is so also. Apparently it is; for they enable the divers to respire equally well by letting down a cauldron; for this does not fill with water, but retains the air, for it is forced down straight into the water; since, if it inclines at all from an upright position, the water flows in. Why do some people cough when they scrape their ears? Is it because the hearing is connected with the same duct as the lungs and the wind-pipe? This is shown by the fact that, if these parts are filled up, a man becomes deaf. When, therefore, heat is set up by the friction, moisture is caused by melting and flows downwards from the duct into the wind-pipe and causes coughing. Why is it that, if a hole is pierced in the left ear, it generally", "notes": [], "markers": [{"kind": "section", "n": "2", "offset": 459}, {"kind": "section", "n": "3", "offset": 1057}, {"kind": "section", "n": "4", "offset": 1259}, {"kind": "section", "n": "5", "offset": 1420}, {"kind": "section", "n": "6", "offset": 2424}, {"kind": "section", "n": "7", "offset": 2803}], "bekker": [{"n": 1, "offset": 0, "real": true},