 "e)pi/"}, {"t": "τῶν", "o": 8, "k": "tw=n"}, {"t": "γνάθων", "o": 12, "k": "gna/qwn"}, {"t": "ἔτι", "o": 20, "k": "e)/ti"}, {"t": "δὲ", "o": 24, "k": "de/"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 27, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "ὅτι", "o": 31, "k": "o(/ti"}, {"t": "λεπτότατον", "o": 35, "k": "lepto/taton"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 46, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "δέρμα", "o": 49, "k": "de/rma"}]}, {"n": 36, "text": "τὸ περιτεταμένον, μάλιστα δὴ φαίνεται δι' αὐτά.", "tokens": [{"t": "τὸ", "o": 0, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "περιτεταμένον", "o": 3, "k": "peritetame/non"}, {"t": "μάλιστα", "o": 18, "k": "ma/lista"}, {"t": "δὴ", "o": 26, "k": "dh/"}, {"t": "φαίνεται", "o": 29, "k": "fai/netai"}, {"t": "δι'", "o": 38, "k": "di'"}, {"t": "αὐτά", "o": 42, "k": "au)ta/"}]}, {"n": 37, "text": "Διὰ τί οὐδεὶς χασμώμενος τὸ οὖς σκαλεύει; ἢ ὅτι ὅτε", "tokens": [{"t": "Διὰ", "o": 0, "k": "dia/"}, {"t": "τί", "o": 4, "k": "ti/"}, {"t": "οὐδεὶς", "o": 7, "k": "ou)dei/s"}, {"t": "χασμώμενος", "o": 14, "k": "xasmw/menos"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 25, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "οὖς", "o": 28, "k": "ou)=s"}, {"t": "σκαλεύει", "o": 32, "k": "skaleu/ei"}, {"t": "ἢ", "o": 42, "k": "h)/"}, {"t": "ὅτι", "o": 44, "k": "o(/ti"}, {"t": "ὅτε", "o": 48, "k": "o(/te"}]}, {"n": 38, "text": "χασμᾶται, ἐμφυσᾶται καὶ ἡ μῆνιγξ, δι' ἧς ἀκούει; σημεῖον", "tokens": [{"t": "χασμᾶται", "o": 0, "k": "xasma=tai"}, {"t": "ἐμφυσᾶται", "o": 10, "k": "e)mfusa=tai"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 20, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "ἡ", "o": 24, "k": "h("}, {"t": "μῆνιγξ", "o": 26, "k": "mh=nigc"}, {"t": "δι'", "o": 34, "k": "di'"}, {"t": "ἧς", "o": 38, "k": "h(=s"}, {"t": "ἀκούει", "o": 41, "k": "a)kou/ei"}, {"t": "σημεῖον", "o": 49, "k": "shmei=on"}]}, {"n": 39, "text": "δέ· ἥκιστα γὰρ ἀκούουσι χασμώμενοι. τὸ γὰρ πνεῦμα, ὥσπερ", "tokens": [{"t": "δέ", "o": 0, "k": "de/"}, {"t": "ἥκιστα", "o": 4, "k": "h(/kista"}, {"t": "γὰρ", "o": 11, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "ἀκούουσι", "o": 15, "k": "a)kou/ousi"}, {"t": "χασμώμενοι", "o": 24, "k": "xasmw/menoi"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 36, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "γὰρ", "o": 39, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "πνεῦμα", "o": 43, "k": "pneu=ma"}, {"t": "ὥσπερ", "o": 51, "k": "w(/sper"}]}, {"n": 40, "text": "καὶ κατὰ τὸ στόμα, καὶ εἰς τὰ ὦτα ἐντὸς πορευόμενον, ἐξωθεῖται", "joined": true, "tokens": [{"t": "καὶ", "o": 0, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "κατὰ", "o": 4, "k": "kata/"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 9, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "στόμα", "o": 12, "k": "sto/ma"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 19, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "εἰς", "o": 23, "k": "ei)s"}, {"t": "τὰ", "o": 27, "k": "ta/"}, {"t": "ὦτα", "o": 30, "k": "w)=ta"}, {"t": "ἐντὸς", "o": 34, "k": "e)nto/s"}, {"t": "πορευόμενον", "o": 40, "k": "poreuo/menon"}, {"t": "ἐξωθεῖται", "o": 53, "k": "e)cwqei=tai"}]}], "english": {"text": "closes up more quickly than in the right ear? It is for this reason that women call the right ear the ‘male’ and the left the ‘female’. Is it because the left parts of the body are moister and hotter, and such things close up very quickly? This is why green plants grow together again; and why wounds close up more readily in the young than in the old. That the parts on the left side of the body are moister is shown by the fact that they are softer and, generally speaking, partake rather of feminine characteristics. Why is it that in those who feel shame the extremities of the ears turn red, but in those who are angry it is the eyes that do so? Is it because shame is a cooling in the eyes accompanied by fear, so that the heat naturally leaves the eyes? So, when it withdraws thence, it travels to the region best adapted to receive it, and this is the extremity of the ears; for the region of the face is otherwise bony. In those who are angry the heat travels in the other direction and makes itself most manifest in the eyes owing to their white colour. Why is it that buzzing in the ears ceases if one makes a sound? Is it because the greater sound drives out the less? Why is it that, if water has flowed into the ear, one pours olive oil in, though the moisture in the ear cannot pass out through another liquid? Is it because the oil floats on the surface of the water and, owing to the adhesive nature of the oil, the water clings to it when it comes out, the object being to make the water come out with the oil? Or is it in order that the ear may be lubricated and the water therefore come out? For oil being smooth acts as a lubricant. Why is it that the ear-drums of divers are less liable to burst if they pour olive-oil beforehand into them? Does the reason for their bursting already mentioned still hold good, but the oil poured into the ears cause the sea-water, which subsequently enters the ear, to glide smoothly over its surface, just as happens on the exterior parts of the bodies of those who anoint themselves? The sea-water gliding smoothly along does not make a violent impact upon the inside of the ear, and so does not break the drum. Why is it that, although the ears are the most bloodless part of the face, they turn red in those who feel shame? Is everything carried to that part which is most devoid of it? Now in a man who feels shame the blood seems to be carried upwards in a heated condition; it therefore passes into the part which is most devoid of it and causes it to become red. The same thing happens also in the cheeks. A further reason is that the skin of the ears, which is tightly stretched, is very thin and therefore very transparent. Why is it that no one scrapes out the ear while yawning? Is it because, when one yawns, the drum of the ear, by means of which he hears, is inflated? That this is so is shown by the fact that one hears least well while yawning; for the breath, as happens also in the mouth, finds its way into the interior of the ears and thrusts the membrane outwards", "notes": [], "markers": [{"kind": "section", "n": "8", "offset": 520}, {"kind": "section", "n": "9", "offset": 1064}, {"kind": "section", "n": "10", "offset": 1181}, {"kind": "section", "n": "11", "offset": 1654}, {"kind": "section", "n": "12", "offset": 2170}, {"kind": "section", "n": "13", "offset": 2690}], "bekker": [{"n": 1, "offset": 0, "real": true}, {"n": 5, "offset": 294, "real": true}, {"n": 10, "offset": 696, "real": true}, {"n": 15, "offset": 996, "real": true}, {"n": 20, "offset": 1302, "real": true}, {"n": 25, "offset": 1712, "real": true}, {"n": 30, "offset": 2110, "real": true}, {"n": 35, "offset": 2570, "real": true}, {"n": 40, "offset": 2918, "real": true}]}}, {"id": "32:961b", "column": "961b", "greek": [{"n": 1, "text": "τὸν ὑμένα καὶ κωλύει τὸν ψόφον εἰσιέναι. ἐὰν οὖν", "tokens": [{"t": "τὸν", "o": 0, "k": "to/n"}, {"t": "ὑμένα", "o": 4, "k": "u(me/na"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 10, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "κωλύει", "o": 14, "k": "kwlu/ei"}, {"t": "τὸν", "o": 21, "k": "to/n"}, {"t": "ψόφον", "o": 25, "k": "yo/fon"}, {"t": "εἰσιέναι", "o": 31, "k": "ei)sie/nai"}, {"t": "ἐὰν", "o": 41, "k": "e)a/n"}, {"t": "οὖν", "o": 45, "k": "ou)=n"}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "οὕτως ἔχοντος ἅψηται τῆς ἀκοῆς ὡς σκαλεύειν, μάλιστ' ἂν", "tokens": [{"t": "οὕτως", "o": 0, "k": "ou(/tws"}, {"t": "ἔχοντος", "o": 6, "k": "e)/xontos"}, {"t": "ἅψηται", "o": 14, "k": "a(/yhtai"}, {"t": "τῆς", "o": 21, "k": "th=s"}, {"t": "ἀκοῆς", "o": 25, "k": "a)koh=s"}, {"t": "ὡς", "o": 31, "k": "w(s"}, {"t": "σκαλεύειν", "o": 34, "k": "skaleu/ein"}, {"t": "μάλιστ'", "o": 45, "k": "ma/list'"}, {"t": "ἂν", "o": 53, "k": "a)/n"}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "βλάψειεν· πρὸς ἀντιπῖπτον γὰρ ἡ πληγὴ γίνεται, καὶ οὐ", "tokens": [{"t": "βλάψειεν", "o": 0, "k": "bla/yeien"}, {"t": "πρὸς", "o": 10, "k": "pro/s"}, {"t": "ἀντιπῖπτον", "o": 15, "k": "a)ntipi=pton"}, {"t": "γὰρ", "o": 26, "k": "ga/r"}, {"t": "ἡ", "o": 30, "k": "h("}, {"t": "πληγὴ", "o": 32, "k": "plhgh/"}, {"t": "γίνεται", "o": 38, "k": "gi/netai"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 47, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "οὐ", "o": 51, "k": "ou)"}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "πρὸς ὑπεῖκον τὸ τοῦ πνεύματος. τὸ δὲ δέρμα καὶ τὴν μήνιγγα", "joined": true, "tokens": [{"t": "πρὸς", "o": 0, "k": "pro/s"}, {"t": "ὑπεῖκον", "o": 5, "k": "u(pei=kon"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 13, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "τοῦ", "o": 16, "k": "tou="}, {"t": "πνεύματος", "o": 20, "k": "pneu/matos"}, {"t": "τὸ", "o": 31, "k": "to/"}, {"t": "δὲ", "o": 34, "k": "de/"}, {"t": "δέρμα", "o": 37, "k": "de/rma"}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 43, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "τὴν", "o": 47, "k": "th/n"}, {"t": "μήνιγγα", "o": 51, "k": "mh/nigga"}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "ἀφεστάναι τῶν στερεῶν δῆλον. ὥστε πόνον μάλιστα", "tokens": [{"t": "ἀφεστάναι", "o": 0, "k": "a)festa/nai"}, {"t": "τῶν", "o": 10, "k": "tw=n"}, {"t": "στερεῶν", "o": 14, "k": "sterew=n"}, {"t": "δῆλον", "o": 22, "k": "dh=lon"}, {"t": "ὥστε", "o": 29, "k": "w(/ste"}, {"t": "πόνον", "o": 34, "k": "po/non"}, {"t": "μάλιστα", "o": 40, "k": "ma/lista"}]}, {"n": 6, "text": "οὕτω ποιεῖ, καὶ τραυματίζοι ἄν.", "tokens": [{"t": "οὕτω", "o": 0, "k": "ou(/tw"}, {"t": "ποιεῖ", "o": 5, "k": "poiei="}, {"t": "καὶ", "o": 12, "k": "kai/"}, {"t": "τραυματίζοι", "o": 16, "k": "traumati/zoi"}, {"t": "ἄν", "o": 28, "k": "a)/n"}]}], "english": {"text": "and prevents the sound from entering. If, therefore, one touches the seat of hearing when in this condition in such a way as to scrape it, one might cause considerable damage to it; for the impact would be against a resisting and unyielding surface inflated by the breath, and it is obvious that the skin and the membrane are far from being solid; and so great pain is caused and a wound might result.", "notes": [], "markers": [], "bekker": [{"n": 1, "offset": 0, "real": true}, {"n": 5, "offset": 283, "real": true}]}}]}